| Purpose                        | Command                          |
| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------- |
| Pull an image                  | `docker pull <image>`            |
| List all images                | `docker images`                  |
| Remove an image                | `docker rmi <image>`             |
| Download image from Docker Hub | `docker pull <username>/<image>` |
| Upload image to Docker Hub     | `docker push <username>/<image>` |




| Purpose                         | Command                                              |
| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| Run container                   | `docker run <image>`                                 |
| Run with name + background mode | `docker run --name <name> -d <image>`                |
| Run & map ports                 | `docker run -p <host_port>:<container_port> <image>` |
| Start a stopped container       | `docker start <container>`                           |
| Stop a running container        | `docker stop <container>`                            |
| Delete a container              | `docker rm <container>`                              |
| Delete container using ID       | `docker rm <id>`                                     |
| List only running containers    | `docker ps`                                          |
| List ALL containers             | `docker ps -a`                                       |
| Restart container automatically | `docker run --restart=always <image>`                |



| Purpose                  | Command                             |
| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |
| Enter container shell    | `docker exec -it <container> sh`    |
| Open Redis CLI (example) | `docker exec -it myredis redis-cli` |
| Exit Redis/CLI           | `exit`                              |


| Purpose                             | Command                         |
| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| View container logs                 | `docker logs <container>`       |
| Monitor CPU/MEM usage               | `docker stats`                  |
| Check container details             | `docker inspect <container>`    |
| See which container uses which port | `docker ps` (check PORT column) |


| Purpose                     | Command                                              |
| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| Build image from Dockerfile | `docker build -t <image_name> .`                     |
| Retag an existing image     | `docker tag <old> <new>`                             |
| Export image to tar         | `docker save -o <file>.tar <image>`                  |
| Create image from container | `docker commit <container_id> <username>/<newimage>` |


| Purpose                | Command         |
| ---------------------- | --------------- |
| Login to Docker Hub    | `docker login`  |
| Logout from Docker Hub | `docker logout` |



| Instruction | Purpose                         |
| ----------- | ------------------------------- |
| `FROM`      | Base image                      |
| `CMD […]`   | Default command to run          |
| `RUN`       | Run shell commands during build |
| `COPY`      | Copy files to image             |
| `WORKDIR`   | Set working directory           |




🟦 Scenario-Based Commands Summary
1. Check running containers
docker ps

2. Stop a container named web_app
docker stop web_app

3. Build image named myapi
docker build -t myapi .

4. Run container exposing port 5000 → 8080
docker run -p 8080:5000 --name web_app -d myapi

5. Enter container shell
docker exec -it <container> sh

6. Delete image old_api
docker rmi old_api

7. Check logs of container
docker logs <container>

8. Run container in background
docker run -d <image>

9. Find which container uses port 3000
docker ps

10. Tag an untagged image
docker tag <image_id> myimage:newtag

11. Export image to tar
docker save -o backup.tar myimage

12. Auto-restart container
docker run --restart=always <image>

13. Check CPU/RAM use
docker stats

13(b). Limit RAM
docker run -m 512m <image>

14. Run shell command before starting app

In Dockerfile:

RUN <your_command>

15. Create custom Nginx image

Dockerfile:

FROM nginx:latest
COPY ./static /usr/share/nginx/html
